      <div class="case-content">
        <section id="audit">
          <h2>1. Empirical telemetry audit findings</h2>
          <p>
            Auditing weeks of real production logs from <code>agent-orchestrator</code> (<code>usage_events.jsonl</code> and <code>telemetry.jsonl</code>) exposed three concrete engineering defects that contradicted optimistic estimates:
          </p>
          <ul>
            <li><strong>7.4× cumulative inflation bug:</strong> <code>agy --resume</code> and <code>codex</code> emit session-cumulative token totals; summing raw turn reports inflated usage metrics and triggered false <code>burn_anomaly</code> alerts.</li>
            <li><strong>MCP adoption gap:</strong> across <strong>10,435 recovered tool calls</strong>, native CLI tools (<code>run_command</code>, <code>read_file</code>) overwhelmingly outnumbered MCP token-saving tools (<code>fs_read_range</code>). Keeping RTK filtering strictly inside MCP left most build/test noise unfiltered.</li>
            <li><strong>Concurrent JSONL gluing (<code>&#125;&#123;</code>):</strong> Rust's <code>writeln!</code> issues two separate <code>write()</code> syscalls (JSON payload + <code>\n</code>), interleaving UI and MCP bridge appends and hiding <code>2,315</code> historical events from line-by-line parsers.</li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <section id="rtk">
          <h2>2. Transparent RTK interception: <code>PreToolUse</code> + <code>PATH</code> shims</h2>
          <p>
            To deliver savings beneath native CLI tools without altering machine-readable output, <code>cli_filter.rs</code> and <code>agent_runner.rs</code> deploy a two-layer interception design:
          </p>
          <ul>
            <li><strong>Claude Code <code>PreToolUse</code> with <code>updatedInput</code>:</strong> an initial <code>PostToolUse</code> prototype appended <code>additionalContext</code> on top of raw tool output (increasing tokens rather than saving them). Replacing it with <code>PreToolUse</code> (<code>--claude-hook</code>, skipped under <code>SafeReadOnly</code>) rewrites simple safe commands to <code>orchestrator-ui --filter-exec &lt;cmd&gt;</code> while preserving every original <code>tool_input</code> key (<code>description</code>, <code>timeout</code>) and rejecting pipes (<code>|</code>), chains (<code>&amp;&amp;</code>), redirects (<code>&gt;</code>), subshells (<code>$(...)</code>), or machine flags (<code>--json</code>, <code>--porcelain</code>).</li>
            <li><strong>Automatic <code>PATH</code> shims (<code>cli_shims/</code>):</strong> <code>spawn_agent_headless</code>, <code>run_delegated_subagent</code>, and <code>spawn_agent_pty</code> prepend shims generated strictly for installed host tools (<code>cargo</code>, <code>npm</code>, <code>pnpm</code>, <code>yarn</code>, <code>pytest</code>, <code>vitest</code>, <code>jest</code>, <code>tsc</code>). Each shim guards against recursion via <code>COCKPIT_FILTER_ACTIVE=1</code> while <code>run_cli_filter_exec</code> strips <code>cli_shims/</code> from child <code>PATH</code> when resolving the real binary. On Windows, <code>git.cmd</code> is intentionally omitted to avoid <code>cmd.exe</code> corrupting <code>%</code> in <code>git log --format</code>, and dual <code>.cmd</code> + POSIX <code>#!/bin/sh</code> shims cover PowerShell, <code>cmd.exe</code>, and Git Bash.</li>
            <li><strong>Verified live measurements:</strong> running unmodified <code>cargo test -p orchestrator-core --lib</code> through the automatic shim compressed <strong><code>1,932 B → 289 B</code> (−85.0%, <code>410</code> tokens saved)</strong>; verbose <code>git status</code> compressed <strong><code>752 B → 435 B</code> (−42.2%, <code>79</code> tokens)</strong>, both logged directly as <code>TokenSaving</code> records.</li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <section id="telemetry">
          <h2>3. Accurate delta telemetry, JSONL file-lock &amp; Observatory</h2>
          <ul>
            <li><strong>Exact session deltas &amp; billing parity (<code>accounts.rs</code>):</strong> subtracts prior cumulative totals on resumed threads and distinguishes OpenAI/Codex billing semantics (<code>input</code> includes cached tokens) from Antigravity/Claude (<code>input</code> excludes cached tokens).</li>
            <li><strong>Locked atomic appends &amp; <code>&#125;&#123;</code> recovery (<code>telemetry.rs</code>):</strong> <code>append_jsonl</code> writes a single contiguous <code>payload + '\n'</code> buffer under an exclusive OS <code>File::lock()</code>; <code>load_jsonl</code> and <code>scripts/build_observatory.py</code> stream-decode legacy glued lines, recovering <code>+2,315</code> events (<code>8,120 → 10,435</code>).</li>
            <li><strong>Measured <code>TokenSaving</code> + Local Observatory:</strong> every byte trimmed by <code>cli_shim</code>, <code>cli_filter</code>, <code>read_dedup</code>, and <code>fs_compact</code> is surfaced in the <code>Usos</code> tab and compiled into <code>docs/cockpit-observatory.html</code> alongside direct <code>:L</code> external editor jump (VS Code/Cursor/Zed) and discarded-hunk telemetry.</li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <section id="failover">
          <h2>4. Hot Auto-Failover, Pre-Flight health, 4G Relay &amp; CI</h2>
          <ul>
            <li><strong>Pre-Flight health &amp; hot Auto-Failover (<code>router.rs</code>, <code>accounts.rs</code>):</strong> checks quota/auth health before dispatch and seamlessly shifts mid-session to a healthy fallback engine with a compact handoff capsule when a provider exhausts credits or rolling limits.</li>
            <li><strong>Extended outage recovery &amp; zero-Tailscale 4G relay (<code>workspace_state.rs</code>):</strong> adds <code>/recover</code> (importing threads from CLI sessions/trash), PC↔Laptop mirror sync, a Cloudflare 4G relay worker, 1-click CLI auto-install via <code>winget</code>, and Android inbox preview, inline images &amp; peer dispatch.</li>
            <li><strong>Zero-downtime Windows self-update &amp; release CI:</strong> <code>apply-self-update.ps1</code> renames the live <code>orchestrator-ui.exe → .old.exe</code> prior to compiling with <code>lto=false</code> and <code>codegen-units=16</code> (preventing <code>0xc0000409</code> OOM and UI stalls), paired with <code>.github/workflows/release.yml</code> for automated Windows + Linux builds.</li>
          </ul>
        </section>

